WEBVTT

NOTE
run: r440fc84a
step: translation
episode: comedy_proof_jinnai_oogiri
source: r10f4bc40_reflow_repaired.vtt
created: 2026-05-02T09:15:00.873565+00:00
target_language: English

00:00:02.681 --> 00:00:07.421
Professor Matsumoto,
Assistant Professor Kotoge,

00:00:07.722 --> 00:00:09.822
thank you for joining us today.

00:00:09.962 --> 00:00:11.262
Thank you.

00:00:11.302 --> 00:00:14.963
Let's get right to it.
Today's test subject is...

00:00:14.983 --> 00:00:15.983
Right.

00:00:18.904 --> 00:00:23.065
Someone everyone knows
and loves: Jinnai.

00:00:23.105 --> 00:00:24.305
We know him. We love him.

00:00:24.425 --> 00:00:28.986
What do you think of Jinnai
as a comedian?

00:00:29.246 --> 00:00:31.726
He's incredibly talented.

00:00:31.926 --> 00:00:32.986
He's funny.

00:00:33.186 --> 00:00:37.747
You could call him a genius
of solo skits.

00:00:37.847 --> 00:00:40.048
He's amazing.

00:00:40.108 --> 00:00:45.309
He makes such funny skits,
but he can't do oogiri at all.

00:00:45.489 --> 00:00:46.669
Really?

00:00:47.289 --> 00:00:47.989
Really?

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:54.051
It made no sense, so once,
over drinks, I asked him why.

00:00:54.131 --> 00:00:58.912
He said, "Because I can't
think of it in advance."

00:00:58.912 --> 00:00:59.912
Right.

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:03.612
"That's why I can't do oogiri.
I just can't do it on the spot."

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:11.694
"If you tell me beforehand,
I won't lose to Bakarhythm."

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:13.954
He went that far?

00:01:14.195 --> 00:01:17.115
"I'm worth about
three Bakarhythms."

00:01:17.395 --> 00:01:20.136
That's what he said:
three Bakarhythms.

00:01:20.136 --> 00:01:23.056
So we thought we'd
try it once,

00:01:23.176 --> 00:01:25.157
and that's why we're
holding this today.

00:01:25.357 --> 00:01:28.777
So Jinnai brought this
on himself.

00:01:28.877 --> 00:01:30.778
Of course he did.

00:01:30.778 --> 00:01:31.758
He asked for it.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:32.918
Not at all.

00:01:33.518 --> 00:01:35.379
Jinnai can't hear us
right now.

00:01:35.519 --> 00:01:36.319
So, with that...

00:01:36.319 --> 00:01:38.879
First, please watch this VTR.

00:01:38.959 --> 00:01:41.100
Right, okay.

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:45.090
This was one week earlier.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:46.540
Yes.

00:01:48.791 --> 00:01:49.791
Thanks for coming.

00:01:49.861 --> 00:01:51.201
Thanks.

00:01:51.641 --> 00:01:52.921
Thanks.

00:01:53.022 --> 00:01:57.282
We're here for DOWNTOWN+'s
Comedy Proof.

00:01:58.442 --> 00:02:01.783
Comedy Proof?
The one Kotoge does?

00:02:01.923 --> 00:02:02.923
That's right.

00:02:02.943 --> 00:02:03.943
Okay.

00:02:07.164 --> 00:02:16.565
You may not remember, but you once said,
"If I had time, I could do oogiri."

00:02:16.565 --> 00:02:17.865
You said that.
- Wow, his face changed. - Huh?

00:02:17.865 --> 00:02:20.645
Your face twisted the second
you heard "oogiri."

00:02:20.813 --> 00:02:22.098
Huh? Matsumoto said that?

00:02:22.986 --> 00:02:24.026
His hands are shaking.

00:02:24.046 --> 00:02:26.026
Huh? Wait. Hold on.

00:02:26.166 --> 00:02:29.227
Uh... oogiri?
What did I say?

00:02:31.107 --> 00:02:33.687
"If I had time,
I could do oogiri."

00:02:33.727 --> 00:02:34.727
Oh.

00:02:34.857 --> 00:02:35.857
No, no... okay.

00:02:36.788 --> 00:02:37.948
I guess... I did say that.

00:02:38.368 --> 00:02:43.248
We were drinking, and it was like,
"You write material, so why can't you?"

00:02:44.529 --> 00:02:52.550
And I just mumbled, "If I had time,
I could do it too."

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:54.690
I didn't mean it that seriously.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:55.450
Is he okay?

00:02:55.450 --> 00:03:00.671
I said it, sure. But how does he remember?
He was still on hiatus then.

00:03:02.911 --> 00:03:07.932
If I get one week for oogiri...
Wait, hold on.

00:03:08.412 --> 00:03:10.832
I told you, I hate this.
I'm bad at it.

00:03:11.792 --> 00:03:15.473
A lot of comedians say,
"Please watch my oogiri."

00:03:15.553 --> 00:03:19.354
They say they're good at it.
I said I hate it. I'm bad at it.

00:03:19.754 --> 00:03:20.494
Right.

00:03:20.494 --> 00:03:22.414
So he asked,
"Why are you bad at it?"

00:03:23.244 --> 00:03:31.075
I just said, "If I had time,
I could do it," like I was arguing back.

00:03:31.075 --> 00:03:32.075
Ah, right.

00:03:32.515 --> 00:03:34.556
So this time,
we brought you some prompts.

00:03:35.736 --> 00:03:36.736
Oh no.

00:03:38.016 --> 00:03:43.658
Recording is exactly
one week from now.

00:03:43.778 --> 00:03:45.698
Huh? One week from now?
So that means...

00:03:47.789 --> 00:03:48.789
You're giving me time?

00:03:49.079 --> 00:03:50.079
That's right.

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:52.150
That raises the bar!

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.120
I don't need this.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.061
You don't have to prove that.

00:03:56.951 --> 00:03:57.951
I don't want people seeing this.

00:03:59.562 --> 00:04:05.483
I don't want anyone to see this!

00:04:05.943 --> 00:04:07.264
But still!

00:04:10.224 --> 00:04:11.585
I write my own material.

00:04:12.525 --> 00:04:13.525
For over 20 years.

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:14.886
Since I went solo.

00:04:15.736 --> 00:04:16.736
I've won awards too.

00:04:17.647 --> 00:04:19.868
So, with enough time...

00:04:21.889 --> 00:04:22.889
I can do okay.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:28.811
So they'll say I spent
a whole week thinking?

00:04:29.641 --> 00:04:30.641
Yes, exactly.

00:04:30.861 --> 00:04:31.861
Oh, so they'll know?

00:04:32.132 --> 00:04:36.153
I can't make it look
improvised?

00:04:37.334 --> 00:04:38.134
No.

00:04:38.134 --> 00:04:43.475
I said I hate this!

00:04:43.475 --> 00:04:45.016
What do you mean, "No"?!

00:04:45.156 --> 00:04:50.098
So he did admit
he said it himself.

00:04:50.238 --> 00:04:53.519
He was really weaselly.

00:04:55.139 --> 00:05:01.421
Even before starting, he had excuses,
and once inside, he tried every trick.

00:05:01.722 --> 00:05:03.462
Only his jacket was white.

00:05:03.522 --> 00:05:06.503
Everything he said was murky.

00:05:08.544 --> 00:05:11.885
Now Jinnai is standing by.
- That's right.

00:05:11.885 --> 00:05:18.067
He's in the green room with answers
he spent a full week thinking through.

00:05:18.307 --> 00:05:19.627
Shall we talk to him now?

00:05:19.627 --> 00:05:20.627
Yes.

00:05:21.608 --> 00:05:22.608
Jinnai!

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:24.028
It's Matsumoto.

00:05:24.269 --> 00:05:25.269
Good morning.

00:05:25.269 --> 00:05:26.249
Good morning.

00:05:26.249 --> 00:05:26.849
Yes.

00:05:26.849 --> 00:05:30.550
It feels like Jinnai
is in good form today.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:32.430
I guess so.

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:34.270
I had a whole week.

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:35.790
I see.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:39.651
Rather than "good form,"
I'm fine. It's okay.

00:05:39.671 --> 00:05:41.971
Kotoge and Fujiwara were
just saying this too,

00:05:42.071 --> 00:05:44.732
but everyone really loves
your material.

00:05:44.898 --> 00:05:46.112
Oh, thank you.

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:47.452
Your solo skits are funny.

00:05:47.452 --> 00:05:48.452
They're funny.

00:05:48.733 --> 00:05:50.213
Sometimes they're incredibly unfunny.

00:05:50.213 --> 00:05:51.653
You don't have to say that.

00:05:51.673 --> 00:05:53.973
You say that a lot,
but you don't have to.

00:05:53.993 --> 00:05:56.594
Maybe one in every twenty
is unfunny.

00:05:56.654 --> 00:05:58.694
That's still an amazing rate.

00:05:58.694 --> 00:05:59.694
Amazing.

00:05:59.754 --> 00:06:02.915
I believe someone like you
has to be able to do oogiri.

00:06:02.915 --> 00:06:03.615
Right.

00:06:03.615 --> 00:06:04.615
Exactly.

00:06:05.035 --> 00:06:07.556
And yes, I did say
if I had time.

00:06:07.556 --> 00:06:08.436
Oh, you did.

00:06:08.436 --> 00:06:10.796
So today, let's wipe
all that away.

00:06:10.956 --> 00:06:11.476
I see.

00:06:11.476 --> 00:06:16.517
If we learn you can do it with time,
I'll never bring up oogiri again.

00:06:16.697 --> 00:06:21.238
Honestly, I found myself thinking,
"Oh, I can do this."

00:06:21.798 --> 00:06:23.278
So you're confident.

00:06:23.838 --> 00:06:24.979
I had some time.

00:06:25.479 --> 00:06:26.219
I see.

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:29.719
I don't want to raise
the bar too much,

00:06:29.759 --> 00:06:33.420
but there is evolution.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:34.760
I see.

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:38.161
And we're not trying
to set you up

00:06:38.921 --> 00:06:43.022
so we can say, "A week passed,
and it still wasn't funny."

00:06:43.022 --> 00:06:43.522
Right.

00:06:43.522 --> 00:06:44.682
This is Comedy Proof.

00:06:44.862 --> 00:06:45.862
We're serious.

00:06:45.862 --> 00:06:48.823
If it's truly funny, I want you
to prove that a week works.

00:06:49.383 --> 00:06:51.523
I actually want you
to prove it. - Yes.

00:06:51.523 --> 00:06:52.523
To me.

00:06:52.803 --> 00:06:53.803
Right?

00:06:53.863 --> 00:06:57.264
Of course. I didn't come here
to get a laugh...

00:06:57.304 --> 00:06:58.124
What did you say?

00:06:58.124 --> 00:06:59.984
Sorry, I stumbled there.

00:07:00.245 --> 00:07:01.065
"To get a laugh."

00:07:01.065 --> 00:07:02.725
That's not why I'm here.

00:07:02.725 --> 00:07:03.965
A phrase we rarely hear.

00:07:04.045 --> 00:07:05.565
I'm not just chasing laughs.

00:07:05.966 --> 00:07:06.966
I want proper laughs.

00:07:07.036 --> 00:07:08.036
Exactly.

00:07:08.036 --> 00:07:09.036
Yes.

00:07:09.286 --> 00:07:15.107
Your material is basically made
of oogiri answers already.

00:07:15.107 --> 00:07:15.947
That's true.

00:07:15.947 --> 00:07:20.668
If you can make that,
you should be able to do this.

00:07:20.668 --> 00:07:21.428
Right.

00:07:21.428 --> 00:07:24.549
If you can't, then a writer
must be making those skits.

00:07:24.629 --> 00:07:27.529
Right. Then you basically
have a writer's brain.

00:07:27.709 --> 00:07:31.470
He does it all himself,
properly.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.430
So for this proof,
we're comparing them, right?

00:07:34.951 --> 00:07:40.592
Of course. We filmed the answers
right after he saw the prompts too.

00:07:40.632 --> 00:07:41.632
I see.

00:07:41.692 --> 00:07:44.252
His answers right after
he heard the prompts a week ago.

00:07:44.252 --> 00:07:45.252
The immediate ones.

00:07:45.473 --> 00:07:50.553
Then we'll see the one-week answers
and compare how much they changed.

00:07:50.553 --> 00:07:57.535
I see.
We also had him answer after three days.

00:07:57.535 --> 00:07:58.095
Oh, really?

00:07:58.095 --> 00:08:02.916
We'll study all three patterns
and see how they change.

00:08:02.916 --> 00:08:03.496
I'm excited.

00:08:03.496 --> 00:08:04.496
Yes.

00:08:06.427 --> 00:08:15.318
The professor wants to see
Jinnai's growth process,

00:08:16.598 --> 00:08:20.039
starting with his immediate answer
and how it changes.

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:21.479
Jinnai is seriously in trouble.

00:08:21.799 --> 00:08:22.799
Day one.

00:08:23.059 --> 00:08:24.760
So this is normal oogiri.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:26.940
Damn it.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:27.940
That was a real tongue click.

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:29.061
This is bad.

00:08:29.061 --> 00:08:35.142
But fine, fine. You're giving me time,
right? I can answer in a week, right?

00:08:35.622 --> 00:08:40.443
My proper answer. Nobody gets an answer
on the first try in oogiri.

00:08:40.643 --> 00:08:45.544
He said proudly,
"No answer on the first try."

00:08:49.124 --> 00:08:53.085
"If there are 30 people,
at least one has one, right?" What?

00:08:53.865 --> 00:08:54.865
It's day one, after all.

00:08:55.045 --> 00:08:56.045
That's right.

00:08:56.685 --> 00:08:58.086
Let me think for just a second.

00:08:58.086 --> 00:08:59.646
I mean, come on.

00:08:59.646 --> 00:09:01.806
"If there are 30 people,
at least one has one." What?

00:09:02.486 --> 00:09:05.687
Anyone would... Maybe I should
just say it right away.

00:09:05.747 --> 00:09:06.747
Right.

00:09:06.967 --> 00:09:09.827
Yeah. If there are 30 people,
at least one has one.

00:09:09.827 --> 00:09:10.707
Junior, maybe?
- Sure, sure.

00:09:10.707 --> 00:09:12.128
Excuse me.
- Thirty people.

00:09:12.128 --> 00:09:15.908
It literally says "day one."

00:09:16.428 --> 00:09:17.548
Is this even oogiri?

00:09:18.389 --> 00:09:20.049
I've never seen this in oogiri.

00:09:20.189 --> 00:09:22.709
Of course I admire people
who can do oogiri.

00:09:23.309 --> 00:09:26.170
But people who like it
can do it themselves.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:27.130
He takes forever to start.

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:28.130
Forever.

00:09:28.650 --> 00:09:32.391
These days, it feels like comedians

00:09:33.131 --> 00:09:36.331
aren't accepted unless
they can do oogiri. I hate that!

00:09:38.139 --> 00:09:39.424
Matsumoto created that culture.

00:09:39.532 --> 00:09:42.092
And I carried it on.

00:09:42.092 --> 00:09:43.512
Wait, if there are 30 people...

00:09:43.952 --> 00:09:45.552
You have to say it.
You can't take this long.

00:09:45.552 --> 00:09:46.293
Right.

00:09:46.293 --> 00:09:47.173
Hold on.

00:09:47.173 --> 00:09:50.373
It's already been 10, 15 minutes.

00:09:50.533 --> 00:09:54.774
Thirty people... At least one of them
has one, right? Come on.

00:09:56.214 --> 00:09:57.034
Uh, 30 people...

00:09:57.034 --> 00:09:58.194
He's not getting there.

00:09:58.854 --> 00:09:59.595
Not at all.

00:09:59.595 --> 00:10:02.315
Okay, this is it. Yeah.

00:10:11.356 --> 00:10:11.916
Huh.

00:10:11.916 --> 00:10:14.117
Maybe that's not it...

00:10:14.577 --> 00:10:15.997
Oh!
- Uh...

00:10:16.297 --> 00:10:18.838
Wait a second.

00:10:18.838 --> 00:10:19.758
Well, it's day one.

00:10:19.758 --> 00:10:20.758
His first try.

00:10:21.198 --> 00:10:23.779
I'm sure this isn't right...
- Okay!

00:10:23.779 --> 00:10:28.920
Okay, okay! That's fine!
Get it out!

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:30.240
If there are 30 people...

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:30.981
Yes.

00:10:30.981 --> 00:10:32.521
at least one has one.

00:10:32.521 --> 00:10:33.221
Yes.

00:10:33.221 --> 00:10:34.661
What?
- Uh, this.

00:10:35.142 --> 00:10:36.142
A Giza-10.

00:10:37.272 --> 00:10:38.272
Thank you.

00:10:38.362 --> 00:10:39.442
Hold on.

00:10:39.442 --> 00:10:40.603
Don't say "thank you"...

00:10:40.603 --> 00:10:41.443
That's so sincere.

00:10:41.443 --> 00:10:43.803
Sincere.

00:10:43.943 --> 00:10:44.924
It's sincere.

00:10:44.924 --> 00:10:46.164
A Giza-10. The 10-yen coin.

00:10:47.044 --> 00:10:51.065
He just answered
the actual question.

00:10:52.305 --> 00:10:55.046
So not as oogiri,
just literally.

00:10:55.046 --> 00:10:56.026
He just answered the question.

00:10:56.026 --> 00:10:57.986
I see. That makes sense.

00:11:03.848 --> 00:11:04.728
IKKO.

00:11:04.728 --> 00:11:05.348
Yes.

00:11:05.348 --> 00:11:09.789
Her final words weren't
"Dondake."

00:11:09.789 --> 00:11:10.789
Right, right.

00:11:10.789 --> 00:11:11.789
What did she say?

00:11:11.789 --> 00:11:12.789
Ah...

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:17.030
Having a model person
makes it easier.

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:17.931
I see.

00:11:17.931 --> 00:11:18.891
Easier to imagine.

00:11:18.891 --> 00:11:19.891
Yes.

00:11:21.271 --> 00:11:24.612
You kind of know
how many syllables it should be.

00:11:24.672 --> 00:11:28.793
Basically, you riff off
"Dondake."

00:11:29.573 --> 00:11:30.573
Right.

00:11:30.573 --> 00:11:31.414
If it's not "Dondake"...

00:11:31.414 --> 00:11:33.654
Is it still "Dondake"?

00:11:33.974 --> 00:11:35.714
Do people use "Dondake"
for this kind of thing?

00:11:36.461 --> 00:11:38.389
Do they all use that rhythm?

00:11:39.335 --> 00:11:42.016
Oh, I see.
You go with "Dondake."

00:11:42.016 --> 00:11:43.016
A born rule-setter.

00:11:43.456 --> 00:11:45.657
With the rules.

00:11:46.377 --> 00:11:47.257
What do I do?

00:11:47.257 --> 00:11:48.557
IKKO. You know IKKO, right?

00:11:48.557 --> 00:11:49.557
That's right.

00:11:49.757 --> 00:11:51.598
IKKO, the beauty expert.

00:11:51.598 --> 00:11:52.598
Yes.

00:11:52.818 --> 00:11:55.759
You know her.
Don't overthink "beauty expert."

00:11:56.459 --> 00:11:57.459
Uh, right.

00:11:57.539 --> 00:11:58.499
Yes.

00:11:58.499 --> 00:11:59.280
Uh...

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:01.620
His pen isn't moving at all.

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:03.420
No way.

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:04.420
Wait a little longer.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:06.220
This is hard.

00:12:07.681 --> 00:12:10.361
Do I use the "Dondake" rhythm?

00:12:10.761 --> 00:12:14.641
Does everyone use "Dondake"
for this?

00:12:14.641 --> 00:12:15.981
Right, right.
- Already?

00:12:18.601 --> 00:12:19.601
Okay, okay.

00:12:20.042 --> 00:12:24.142
IKKO's final words
were not "Dondake."

00:12:24.582 --> 00:12:25.222
What did she say?

00:12:25.222 --> 00:12:26.002
Okay, here!

00:12:26.002 --> 00:12:27.002
Thanks a lot.

00:12:27.622 --> 00:12:28.622
Oh.

00:12:30.363 --> 00:12:31.363
Thank you.

00:12:32.083 --> 00:12:35.523
I think you really should
keep it to four syllables.

00:12:35.523 --> 00:12:36.523
Right.

00:12:37.143 --> 00:12:39.843
You should at least keep
those four beats of "Dondake."

00:12:40.243 --> 00:12:42.564
"Thank you" would've worked.

00:12:43.024 --> 00:12:47.044
Tomonori Jinnai's third prompt.

00:12:49.264 --> 00:12:53.164
"This person has to be strong
in a fight." What name?

00:12:54.905 --> 00:12:56.245
Okay.
- Oh, this one.

00:12:56.245 --> 00:12:57.245
Ah.

